{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1528234-wtf-2e-what-if-the-firstborn-reunited-and-forsaken-pure-became-one\u2026","id":1528234,"title":"WtF 2E: What if the Firstborn reunited and Forsaken/Pure became one\u2026","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-08T17:10:55-08:00","id":1528234,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> WtF 2E: What if the Firstborn reunited and Forsaken/Pure became one\u2026","content":"I\u2019m playing a Storm Lord/Rahu in a great chronicle and I\u2019ve decided to take on a righteous/dangerous quest in attempts to truly bring The People together as a whole, to include the Firstborn. So far I\u2019ve met an ancient wolf spirit, a fleshly ancestor from the time of Pangea, obtained an ancient book of history along with ancient Wolf armor and learned the truth behind Father Wolf\u2019s death. It\u2019s just me and my Storm Lord/Itheaur comrade for now, as we had to leave our pack behind to protect them from what\u2019s coming for us, once this quest really gains momentum\u2026<br /> <br /> What kind of internal or external challenges do you think I could face along the way in this long journey???<br /> <br /> #IndulgeMeIfYouWill \ud83d\ude01 (Note: 1st post was flagged. This is not spam)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11532,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11532-dpowell","user":"DPowell","date":". 01-08-2024, 08:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11532-dpowell","name":"DPowell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11532_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-08T17:27:26-08:00","id":1528235,"title":"","content":"This is far outside of the typical for a game, so it will be extremely DM dependent. <br /> <br /> Assassins are a given, as is pretty much anything else you can think of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-08T18:07:33-08:00","id":1528237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DPowell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1528234-wtf-2e-what-if-the-firstborn-reunited-and-forsaken-pure-became-one\u2026#post1528234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m playing a Storm Lord/Rahu in a great chronicle and I\u2019ve decided to take on a righteous/dangerous quest in attempts to truly bring The People together as a whole, to include the Firstborn. So far I\u2019ve met an ancient wolf spirit, a fleshly ancestor from the time of Pangea, <b>obtained an ancient book of history along with ancient Wolf armor and learned the truth behind Father Wolf\u2019s death.</b> It\u2019s just me and my Storm Lord/Itheaur comrade for now, as we had to leave our pack behind to protect them from what\u2019s coming for us, once this quest really gains momentum\u2026<br /> <br /> What kind of internal or external challenges do you think I could face along the way in this long journey???<br /> <br /> #IndulgeMeIfYouWill \ud83d\ude01 (Note: 1st post was flagged. This is not spam)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> What truth did you learn about Father Wolf death? Depending on your version, you will have believers, oppositors and people ignoring you.<br /> <br /> <br /> It is unlikely to work just on your say so. What would make you better than the others (both Pure and Forsaken) that have tried to merge the camps? What tends to work is to have a third party as enemy, look at the write-up of the THE FALSE FATHER \u2014 LUL\u2019AYA, in the 2ed Core book, it is one of the few things that make everyone agree to join hands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-08T18:57:00-08:00","id":1528240,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4967_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4967\" data-vbnamecard=\"4967\">lbeaumanior</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What truth did you learn about Father Wolf death? Depending on your version, you will have believers, oppositors and people ignoring you.<br /> <br /> It is unlikely to work just on your say so. What would make you better than the others (both Pure and Forsaken) that have tried to merge the camps? What tends to work is to have a third party as enemy, look at the write-up of the THE FALSE FATHER \u2014 LUL\u2019AYA, in the 2ed Core book, it is one of the few things that make everyone agree to join hands </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve read the False Father story. It\u2019s great &amp; very twisted.<br /> <br /> In my current chronicle, an Abyssal spirit has invaded Seattle and infested nearly the entire Shadow of the city. I was able to pull off convincing The Pure to join forces with us and I put in motion a strategy to banish the Abyssal invader. I plan to build on that momentary truce in Seattle to serve as a testing ground and grow things from there if I\u2019m successful.<br /> <br /> As for Father Wolf\u2019s death, I learned that the Pure were right (FW didn\u2019t need to die nor was he losing his edge) however there was a deeper treachery (murdering FWs actual first litter to be on top) that the Pure totems took part in that led to the Forsaken totems killing Father Wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11532,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11532-dpowell","user":"DPowell","date":". 01-08-2024, 10:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11532-dpowell","name":"DPowell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11532_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-08T20:33:30-08:00","id":1528246,"title":"","content":"I would say that this endeavor would be virtually impossible personally, the Pure Totems would never willingly agree to rejoin with their Forsaken siblings, and the culture of the Pure makes re-integrating with the Urdaga in any way beyond every Forsaken Tribe dissolving and converting to the Fire-Touched or Predator Kings immeasurably unlikely.<br /> <br /> but if you could think of some sort of world-shattering threat that could cause all Uratha tribes to put aside their differences and come together as a titanic spiritual monoculture.. I\u2019d love to hear what you concoct!<br /> <br /> edit: Your idea is interesting, but I dunno if it would be quite enough to truly unite the species. They are immensely clannish and fractious and I could see most Uratha straight up not believing this truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 01-08-2024, 11:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-09T02:28:55-08:00","id":1528248,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1686_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1686\" data-vbnamecard=\"1686\">Korogra</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> edit: Your idea is interesting, but I dunno if it would be quite enough to truly unite the species. They are immensely clannish and fractious and I could see most Uratha straight up not believing this </div> </div> </div>To expand on my quest a bit, I\u2019d pitch that everyone remain in their respective tribes but leave the Forsaken/Pure culture behind and forge ahead anew with mindfulness of boundaries, to focus on a Greater Hunt (probably become a threat to those who\u2019ve enjoyed a world without FW &amp; his children as a single force on the prowl) to truly take up the ancestral duties as a united front, which the world hasn\u2019t seen in eons. Regarding the truth I\u2019ve learned, I\u2019m still meditating on what exactly to share and what the fallout could look like as this has the potential to fail horribly. I\u2019m also seeking the knowledge on how exactly our ancestors bound our totems and how I might convince them to call a truce, with aid from Lunes and/or Helion. Lastly, Ive learned that a Fire Touched NPC (King Maker) of age in Seattle is in possession of a crown that has the power to bring all Uratha under sway should the wearer be worthy. If I can wrestle it from him and find out how to become worthy then I\u2019m set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11532,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11532-dpowell","user":"DPowell","date":". 01-09-2024, 05:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11532-dpowell","name":"DPowell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11532_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-10T11:47:14-08:00","id":1528336,"title":"","content":"One challenge would be all the fools and heretics that've tried this quest before, with different beliefs and methodologies of how such a shift in culture could be accomplished that're fundamentally incompatible with your own. Bale Hounds, also, could be playing at this quest from any and all sides - an expanding territory of unified Uratha Tribes, riddled with <i>Asah Gadar</i> manipulators in the shadows in secret correspondence between each other. And many spirit patrons would have interests in ensuring that the Forsaken and Pure Tribes remain in conflict with each other, as ancient spirits that've survived into the modern age tend to enjoy the freedom that came with Urfarah's death and the division of the people responsible for policing them, not to mention the benefits that powerful spirits enjoy from Anshega reverence and deference.<br /> <br /> The variety of different Lodges that emerged could feel threatened by the idea of bringing Urdaga and Anshega together, as it compromises the existence of many of them and their spiritual patrons in turn. A couple of them might support and condone a unification of Pure and Forsaken... conditionally, hunting under the guidance and purpose bestowed by a specific spirit that believes it can maintain such a balance on a Lodge's limited scale. If the divisions between the Firstborn were healed, Lodges on either side, between, and outside of the conflict may feel a sense of existential crisis as they would be forced to either adapt or die when they've already cultivated the Sacred Hunt in specific ways, or that their Lodge culture could be threatened to change too drastically.<br /> <br /> Blood Talons would face a uniquely difficult time, because the core of their Tribe is the Sacred Hunt of Uratha, and the potential for unity could spark difficulties and tension for everyone involved. Maybe the Blood Talons would feel insulted or compromised that their sacred prey suddenly became far more restricted to hunt for the sake of 'peace' and 'unification', maybe some Blood Talons agree with the ideal of unification between the Forsaken and Pure Tribes <i>only</i> if they were at the top to enforce both groups with their Sacred Hunt, Pure who're more tolerant of the idea of peace with their former enemies would certainly criticize and distrust Blood Talons to some extent as the hunting of werewolves is a fundamental element of their existence. Likewise, Ivory Claws' culture is rife with scary forms of elitism and many would feel that a potential unity with the Forsaken Tribes could open the door for degeneracy and the weakening of their cultivated bloodlines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23800-the-firebrand","name":"The Firebrand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-11T12:45:48-08:00","id":1528388,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23800-the-firebrand\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23800_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23800\" data-vbnamecard=\"23800\">The Firebrand</a><br /> <br /> WOW, this is some great context and framework for my chronicle. I hadn\u2019t even thought about some of this stuff. I sent your post to my ST for reference. Gonna be a hell-of-a ride, win or lose. One more question for ya. What external (outside of WtF) threats do you think I might face??? \ud83c\udf7f","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11532,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11532-dpowell","user":"DPowell","date":". 01-11-2024, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11532-dpowell","name":"DPowell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11532_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-11T15:55:53-08:00","id":1528400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DPowell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1528234-wtf-2e-what-if-the-firstborn-reunited-and-forsaken-pure-became-one\u2026?p=1528388#post1528388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23800-the-firebrand\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23800_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23800\" data-vbnamecard=\"23800\">The Firebrand</a><br /> <br /> WOW, this is some great context and framework for my chronicle. I hadn\u2019t even thought about some of this stuff. I sent your post to my ST for reference. Gonna be a hell-of-a ride, win or lose. One more question for ya. What external (outside of WtF) threats do you think I might face??? \ud83c\udf7f</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you and your ST enjoyed! As for external threats, I'm mostly working in the basis of what I'm most familiar with in Forsaken 2E and there are no conflicts of interests outside of that which I think would be as consequential, if they can even comprehend werewolf culture enough to understand what 'Forsaken' and 'Pure' mean or that different tribes even exist at all and what the significance of 'unification' would be. That said, the local Kindred demesne might get uppity if they feel their hunting grounds and preferred targets have become increasingly hampered as a consequence of truces and alliances between Urdaga and Anshega to protect their human loved ones, wolf-blooded, and future prey, or if the unified territory has concentrated its efforts to keep vampires from feeding and using their powers in specific places to keep the spirit ecology stable.<br /> <br /> Both the Pentacle Orders and the Seers of the Throne might have something to say about Uratha unification: for the former, largely interest and curiosity to witness and document the potentially existential consequences of such an event, such as having first-hand encounters with one or more Firstborn or finding hard evidence of Urfarah; for the latter, it would have to be determined whether an Uratha unification threatens the Seers' agendas in any significant manner or if a Seer receives prophetic dreams from one of the Exarchs of what the ramifications of such an event could mean. At the most basic level, I could see the God-Machine having Angels masquerading as spirits to keep the status quo of the tribes in place, both because the Uratha are easier to control, monitor, analyse etc. as a fractured people and because a potential unification might threaten or compromise Infrastructure in some way - increased coordination and communication between werewolf groups could spell terrible consequences, where healthy competition and distrust kept things in line just fine.<br /> <br /> Back in WtF, if you want potential threats to your cause that aren't explicitly werewolf in nature, you could have Lunes that straight up don't accept the potential for peace with werewolves who rejected and tore away Mother Luna's auspices and who regularly hunted and killed Lunes up to this point. The <i>Idigam</i> would be easier to hunt with the unification of the tribes, which provides a material rationale on top of their alien logic and comprehension to smite the children of Father Wolf before they can set aside their differences. Void spirits, and their terrestrial cultists and accomplices, would find potential invasions far more difficult in a territory where Forsaken and Pure are in good communication and know they can find a joint threat to their existence beyond the sky. And the funniest option would be Helios taking issue with your cause, purely out of spite against Urfarah's killers and to remind you that whatever earthly affairs you have in mind, your 'peace' cannot undo what has been set in stone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23800-the-firebrand","name":"The Firebrand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}